      "hints": [
        "In an arithmetic progression, the common difference is constant: $u_2 - u_1 = u_3 - u_2$.",
        "Set up the equation $6k - k = (k + 6) - 6k$ and solve for $k$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the common difference property of consecutive terms in an arithmetic progression:\n$$u_2 - u_1 = u_3 - u_2 \\implies 6k - k = (k + 6) - 6k$$",
        "Simplify and solve the linear equation for $k$:\n$$5k = 6 - 5k \\implies 10k = 6 \\implies k = \\frac{6}{10} = \\frac{3}{5} = 0.6$$"
      ],
